-- title:
--   Proof of Theorem 14, first sentence — the conditional moment identity $\mathbb E[e^{\lambda Y_j}\mid\mathcal F_{j-1}]=1+q_A(e^{\lambda u_A}-1)+q_B(e^{\lambda u_B}-1)$
-- statement:
--   Consider a routed run with credits $u_A,u_B>0$, let $\lambda>0$, and let $Y_j=u_{\rho_j}a_j$ be the credit of round $j$. With $q_X=\mathbb P[\rho_j=X\wedge a_j=1\mid\mathcal F_{j-1}]$, almost surely
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb E\bigl[e^{\lambda Y_j}\mid\mathcal F_{j-1}\bigr]=1+q_A\bigl(e^{\lambda u_A}-1\bigr)+q_B\bigl(e^{\lambda u_B}-1\bigr).
--   $$
--
--   Moreover, if $\mathcal Q$ is a soundness profile of the run for $N$ rounds and $j\le N$, then almost surely $\mathbb E[e^{\lambda Y_j}\mid\mathcal F_{j-1}]\le\Lambda_{\mathcal Q}(\lambda)$.
--
--   This is the per-round input to the tail bound of Lemma 1 in the proof of Theorem 14.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: every prover interacting with the verifier on a false statement → every probability space $(\Omega,\mu)$, every filtration $(\mathcal F_j)$, every family of post-base-stage σ-algebras $\mathcal G_j$ and every adapted run $(\rho,a)$ (`IsRoutedRun`); reason: the run of any prover is such a run, with $\mathcal F_j$ generated by the first $j$ rounds and $\mathcal G_j$ by $\mathcal F_{j-1}$ and $\nu_j$; the theorem specializes to the paper's
--   - encoding: the hypothesis $x\notin L$ → not modelled; reason: the run is the run on a false statement; the hypotheses (H0), (HA) and the forgery bound are what $x\notin L$ supplies
--   - encoding: rounds $j=1,\dots,N$ conditioned on $\mathcal F_{j-1}$, answers $a_j\in\{0,1\}$ → 0-based rounds $j<N$ conditioned on `F j`, answers in `Bool`; reason: relabelling; same instances
--   - encoding: $\mathbb P[S\ge\tau]$ and conditional probabilities $\mathbb P[E\mid\mathcal F]$ almost surely → `μ.real {ω | τ ≤ creditSum …}` and `condProb` (Mathlib `condExp` of the indicator), with `∀ᵐ`; reason: Lean convention; the events are measurable, so these are the paper's quantities
-- source:
--   Dumlu, Signal-Routed Two-Arm Verification, STOC 2027 submission manuscript (held version, sha256 d56b3b7a…), proof of Theorem 14, first sentence, p.7

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SigRoute_IsProfile

namespace SigRoute

open MeasureTheory

/-- The conditional moment identity in the proof of Theorem 14 (Dumlu, Signal-Routed Two-Arm Verification, STOC 2027 submission manuscript (held version, sha256 d56b3b7a…), proof of Theorem 14, first
sentence, p.7): with `Y_j = u_{ρ_j} a_j`,
`E[e^{λY_j} | F_{j−1}] = 1 + q_A(e^{λu_A} − 1) + q_B(e^{λu_B} − 1)`, where
`q_X = P[ρ_j = X ∧ a_j = 1 | F_{j−1}]`; and if `Q` is a soundness profile of the run for `N` rounds and
`j < N`, this is `≤ Λ_Q(λ)`. Both hold almost surely.

**Formalization Note** The paper's "every prover" is "every probability space `(Ω, μ)`, filtration `F`, post-base-stage σ-algebras `G` and adapted run `(ρ, a)`" (`IsRoutedRun`); rounds are 0-based, so the paper's `F_{j−1}` is `F j`. -/
theorem theorem_14_mgf_step {Ω : Type*} {m : MeasurableSpace Ω} (μ : Measure Ω)
    [IsProbabilityMeasure μ] (F : Filtration ℕ m) (G : ℕ → MeasurableSpace Ω)
    (ρ : ℕ → Ω → Arm) (a : ℕ → Ω → Bool) (hrun : IsRoutedRun F G ρ a)
    (u : Arm → ℝ) (hu : ∀ X, 0 < u X) (lam : ℝ) (hlam : 0 < lam) (j : ℕ) :
    (condExp (F j) μ (fun ω => Real.exp (lam * stepCredit u ρ a j ω)) =ᵐ[μ] fun ω =>
        1 + condProb μ (F j) {ω | ρ j ω = Arm.A ∧ a j ω = true} ω * (Real.exp (lam * u Arm.A) - 1)
          + condProb μ (F j) {ω | ρ j ω = Arm.B ∧ a j ω = true} ω
              * (Real.exp (lam * u Arm.B) - 1)) ∧
    ∀ (N : ℕ) (Q : Set (ℝ × ℝ)), IsProfile μ F ρ a N Q → j < N →
      ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, condExp (F j) μ (fun ω => Real.exp (lam * stepCredit u ρ a j ω)) ω ≤ Lam u Q lam := by sorry

end SigRoute
